\documentclass{article}
\title{Concatenated Codes Versus Surface Codes}
\author{N. Achterberg}
\date{February 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Overhead}
Fault tolerant quantum computation pays a steep overhead in physical qubits.
We compare Shor & Steane style concatenated codes against the surface code
under a circuit level depolarising noise model,
tracking the logical failure rate as the physical error rate is reduced.
Concatenated constructions win at extremely low noise,
but the surface code dominates in the regime of current hardware.
\end{document}

